Z||000003||Urchin||08-28-2001||12:20 AM||||Well from my experiences my first instinct would be to check the fuel pump.  If you turn the key forward (first position, not to turn it over), you should be able to hear the humm of the pump kicking in at your console.  If it simply is clicking when you try to turn it on then perhaps you need a new starter.  I suppose I'm not answering your intended question though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I would say what it is worth depends on what is wrong with it.  I'll tell you this though, I have over $5000 into mine in replacement parts (suspension/engine, etc.) and I have been having the damndest time selling mine for $2000ish.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroburton||08-28-2001||12:31 AM||||well sence im such a big fan of fieros i will probly keep it (unless some body wants to trade for a running one).<BR>but im getting sick of shelling money off into my car ! it not as bad as all my moms fords but its getting close! how much will this bullshit cost me  ? and does any body have a good  place to take a fiero to to have it looked at when it needs repairs (unlike madas) ?<BR>thanx||||reg||1
Z||000005||Urchin||08-28-2001||12:41 AM||||Cost depends on whether you are getting new or used parts.  I had a new starter put in mine for a little over $200 Cdn.  Fuel pump was slightly more than that.  Used parts are obviously cheaper but short term guarentee (if any).  It might be wise to invest in a parts car if you have the means to do so.  <BR>I went halves on a parts car with a friend of mine.  Cut the cost in half and help each other do the work.  ||||reg||1
